WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.700
A storm cloud hangs high
above a quiet street.

2
00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.970
A raindrop breaks free,
and starts to fall.

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.240
Down it comes, past the rooftops,
all the way to the street.

4
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:13.870
Gravity pulls on it the whole way.

5
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.790
So why doesn't it hit
the ground like a bullet?

6
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.530
In this mission, you'll meet drag: the
force on anything moving through a liquid

7
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:22.800
or a gas.

8
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.690
Then you'll catch a 0.20 kg
ball partway through its fall,

9
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.900
and calculate its
acceleration at that instant.

10
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:35.510
Your mission: explain why raindrops from
high clouds don't hit the ground like

11
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.360
bullets.
